================================================================================
                        APTECH ePROJECT SUBMISSION - README
================================================================================
Project Title : EduPredict - Big Data & Predictive Analytics Platform
Architecture  : React 19 + TypeScript (Frontend) | Python Flask + MongoDB (Backend)
Big Data Stack: Hadoop HDFS, PySpark / MapReduce, Apache Impala SQL, RStudio, Jupyter
Database      : MongoDB (Database: edupredict_db)
================================================================================

1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
-------------------
EduPredict is a comprehensive Big Data and Machine Learning educational analytics
platform designed to improve student retention, optimize academic resource
allocation, and personalize learning interventions.

2. ASSUMPTIONS MADE IN THIS PROJECT
-----------------------------------
1. Hybrid Local Execution & Resilience:
   - The application connects directly to a local MongoDB instance at
     `mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/edupredict_db` via the Python Flask REST API
     (`backend/app.py` on port 5000).
   - If the local MongoDB daemon or Hadoop cluster nodes are offline during a
     classroom demonstration, the system includes an automatic resilient
     simulation mode so all dashboards, SQL queries, and ML predictions remain
     100% interactive without crashing.

2. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):
   - Four distinct institutional roles are implemented and enforced:
     * Administrator (Dean / Academic Affairs)
     * Faculty / Teacher (Course Instructors & Advisors)
     * Student (Personal Academic Pathway & Safe Absences Calculator)
     * Big Data & ML Analyst (HDFS, MapReduce/Spark, Impala SQL, ML Simulator)

3. CSV Data Ingestion & Auto-ID Generation:
   - Uploaded CSV datasets (`StudentID,Name,Email,Department,Semester,AttendanceRate,CurrentGPA,MidtermsAvg,LMSWeeklyHours`)
     are validated in real time.
   - If `StudentID` is left blank in Excel, the system automatically assigns a
     new unique Student ID (`STU-2026-XXXX`), calculates the student's ML dropout
     risk and K-Means cluster, and syncs the records to MongoDB (`edupredict_db`).

4. Big Data & Data Science Deliverables Included in Repository:
   - `/backend/`            : Python Flask REST API (`app.py`), MongoDB ODM schemas (`mongodb_models.py`), and database seeder (`db_seed.py`).
   - `/big_data_pipeline/`  : Hadoop HDFS ingestion bash script (`hdfs_ingest.sh`), PySpark ETL job (`pyspark_etl_job.py`), and Apache Impala DDL/queries (`impala_ddl_and_queries.sql`).
   - `/machine_learning/`   : Jupyter Anaconda Notebook (`EduPredict_ML_and_EDA.ipynb`), Scikit-Learn training pipeline (`train_dropout_model.py`), Anomaly Detector (`anomaly_detector.py`), and RStudio statistical script (`r_statistical_analysis.R`).
   - `/database/`           : MongoDB shell seed script (`mongodb_seed.js`), Tableau dataset (`edupredict_tableau_dataset.csv`), and sample CSV upload batch (`new_students_batch_2026.csv`).

3. HOW TO RUN THE PROJECT (WINDOWS)
-----------------------------------
Option A (One-Click):
  Double-click `run_local.bat` in the project root folder.

Option B (Manual via VS Code Terminal):
  Terminal 1 (Python Backend - Port 5000):
    cd backend
    python -m venv venv
    .\venv\Scripts\activate
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    python db_seed.py
    python app.py

  Terminal 2 (React Frontend - Port 3000):
    npm install
    npm run dev

